Provenance
----------
This port was written from scratch against the behaviour of the original program. It follows the
original's algorithms and constants (the semitone pitch axis, mu-law display scaling, the
120-ticks-per-second SMPTE time grid, the per-tick mean-absolute waveform envelope, the
wavetable tone generator), but it does not contain source code from the C++ version.

In particular it contains no code from the libraries the original bundled or adapted:

  - FFTW 2.x            (GPL)                 replaced by the small FFT in src/core/fft.ts
  - "A Programmer's Guide to Sound" code by Tim Kientzle, 1997 (BSD-style licence with an
    advertising clause)                       replaced by the browser's own audio decoding
  - CWaveForm, a Win32 waveOut wrapper (Direct Line Corp., 1999-2000)
                                              replaced by the Web Audio API

The original program began as a project for CMPT 365 (Multimedia Systems) at Simon Fraser
University.

Runtime dependencies: none. The shipped app is plain TypeScript compiled by Vite. Development
tools (Vite, TypeScript, Vitest) are used only to build and test it.
